// test_program.hex
//
// 37-word RV32I test program, extracted from the design report (Listing 4,
// "the Hex loaded into IM"). It is the machine code of the C test program in
// Listing 3 (ori/add/sub/addi/or/and/xor/sll/srl/sra/sw/lw/bne/jal...).
//
// NOTE on word 33 (0x01cd8863): the report's C listing shows "bne x28, x27, _jtest"
// while the hex decodes to "beq x27, x28, +16". Both are logically the same
// branch (jump when x27 == x28); the hex is the actual executed code.
//
// Words 29-31 and 34-36 are padding (ori x0, x1, 0 NOPs).
